clean_summary:
Wow, this tweet went very viral! I wanted to share a possibly slightly improved version of the tweet in an 'idea file.' The idea of the idea file is that in this era of LLM agents, there is less need to share specific code or apps; you just share the idea, and the other person's agent customizes and builds it for your specific needs.

Here's the idea in a gist format: you can give this to your agent, and it can build you your own LLM wiki and guide you on how to use it. It's intentionally kept a little abstract because there are many directions to take this in, and people can adjust the idea or contribute their own in the discussion.

@karpathy: "Something I'm finding very useful recently: using LLMs to build personal knowledge bases for various topics of research interest. In this way, a large fraction of my recent token throughput is going less into manipulating code and more into manipulating knowledge (stored as markdown and images). The latest LLMs are quite good at it..."

